      "message": "catch and throws as IllegalArgumentException to keep the current behavior of ConnectivityManager#replaceFirewallChain API\nhttp://cs/aosp-master/packages/modules/Connectivity/framework/src/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java;l\u003d5962;rcl\u003dba5e501b0952f43aa2af144c81de0852b309a881\n\nCurrently, ConnectivityService throws IllegalArgumentException\nhttp://cs/aosp-master/packages/modules/Connectivity/service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java;l\u003d11436;rcl\u003dba5e501b0952f43aa2af144c81de0852b309a881\nBut I removed this unnecessary conversion from int firewall chain type to string firewall chain type in ConnectivityService.\nSo, I made replaceUidChain to throw IllegalArgumentException if chain is not a valid chain.\n\nI\u0027m not sure catch and throw is a good.\nUpdating getMatchByFirewallException to throw IAE or SSE, like below, might be better?\n```\n    public long getMatchByFirewallChain(final int chain, final boolean throwIaeAsSse) {\n        switch (chain) {\n            case FIREWALL_CHAIN_DOZABLE:\n                return DOZABLE_MATCH;\n....\n            default:\n                if (throwIaeAsSse) {\n                    throw new ServiceSpecificException();\n                } else {\n                    throw new IllegalArgumentException();\n                }\n        }\n    }\n```",
